DECL	{"assumptions":[],"binders":["subject"],"id":"NRS_484B_267_2d","intentions":[],"laws":["NRS-484B-267-2d"],"narrowings":[{"kind":"no_atom","span":"s3","why":"The borrowed words of s4 ('at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front'), which the record reads as a lit sig.warning_lamp red, flashing, facing front: no formula can read a lamp's facing. The formula surface of sig_warning_lamp takes a colour, or a colour and a mode, only (Semantics.evalAtomE: [x, col] or [x, col, m]; atomArgSorts admits at most two literal positions for sig_*), so 'facing front' / 'visible from the front' cannot be stated. Colour red and mode flashing are written; the facing is not, so the trigger as written is weaker than the record's (a lamp lit red and flashing facing only the rear or side would engage it). Either the plan re-maps s3 to a red flashing lamp and files 'visible from the front' as a gap, or Core gives sig_warning_lamp a facing literal."}],"operationalizations":[],"residues":["'including, without limitation' lists examples of a vehicle moving or preparing to move; the duty is the same whether or not the vehicle is arriving at or leaving the scene of a crash or other incident"],"surrogate":false}
